# Convenience alias: the no-extension API path 301s to the canonical .json URL.
/api/v1/projection   /api/v1/projection.json   301

# NOTE: there is deliberately no `/*  /index.html  200` SPA fallback here.
#
# That rule made Cloudflare answer EVERY unknown path with the homepage at
# HTTP 200 — a soft 404 across the entire URL space, and a page whose canonical
# pointed at "/" no matter what was requested. It is not needed: the Vite
# prerender plugin writes a real file for every route in ROUTE_META, the
# pipeline writes one per state, and both /embed/* trees are emitted too, so
# every valid path is a static asset that Pages serves at its clean URL.
# Anything left over genuinely does not exist and now gets public/404.html
# with a real 404 status.
#
# If you add a route to App.tsx, add it to ROUTE_META — routeMeta.coverage
# tests fail otherwise, and without a prerendered file the route would 404.
